## Components (`/components`)

### Core Layout Components

| Component | File | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| **Navbar** | [navbar.tsx](file:///d:/Next.js-projects/answarly/components/navbar.tsx) | Sticky top navigation with logo, page links (Home, Topics, History, Leaderboard, Q&A, Quiz), global search trigger, language toggle, theme toggle, login/logout, and avatar dropdown. Responsive — collapses into a dropdown menu on mobile. Polls `localStorage` for user session data. |
| **ConditionalFooter** | [conditional-footer.tsx](file:///d:/Next.js-projects/answarly/components/conditional-footer.tsx) | Footer with branding and copyright. Automatically **hides itself** on auth pages (`/login`, `/signup`) and the quiz results page to keep those views clean. |
| **SmoothScroll** | [smooth-scroll.tsx](file:///d:/Next.js-projects/answarly/components/smooth-scroll.tsx) | Invisible component that sets `scroll-behavior: smooth` on `<html>` at mount. Restores the previous value on unmount. |

---

### i18n & Theming

| Component | File | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| **LanguageProvider** | [i18n.tsx](file:///d:/Next.js-projects/answarly/components/i18n.tsx) | React context provider for **English/Arabic** internationalization. Contains full dictionaries (`en`, `ar`) for nav, hero, topics, login, Q&A, history, and footer strings. Persists language choice in `localStorage` and sets `dir="rtl"` when Arabic is active. Exposes `useI18n()` hook. |
| **LanguageToggle** | [language-toggle.tsx](file:///d:/Next.js-projects/answarly/components/language-toggle.tsx) | Pill button toggling between **EN** and **AR**. Calls `setLang()` from the i18n context. Renders a skeleton-safe fallback before mount to prevent hydration mismatches. |
| **ThemeToggle** | [theme-toggle.tsx](file:///d:/Next.js-projects/answarly/components/theme-toggle.tsx) | Animated sun/moon icon button for **dark ↔ light** theme. Reads and writes to `localStorage` under key `answerly-theme`. Directly toggles the `.dark` class on `<html>` for instant visual feedback with transition animations between icons. |
| **ThemeProvider** | [theme-provider.tsx](file:///d:/Next.js-projects/answarly/components/theme-provider.tsx) | Thin wrapper around `next-themes`'s `ThemeProvider`. Used in the site layout to enable system-level theme detection. |

---

### Animation & Effects

| Component | File | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| **Reveal** | [reveal.tsx](file:///d:/Next.js-projects/answarly/components/reveal.tsx) | Scroll-triggered entrance animation. Uses `IntersectionObserver` (threshold: 0.2) to fade-in + translate-up children. Accepts optional `delay` prop for staggered reveals. Respects `prefers-reduced-motion` for accessibility. GPU-accelerated via `transform-gpu`. |
| **GradientLoader** | [gradient-loader.tsx](file:///d:/Next.js-projects/answarly/components/gradient-loader.tsx) | SVG spinner with a **purple → indigo → pink** gradient stroke. Configurable `size` prop. Used as an inline loading indicator (e.g., inside the search modal). |

---

### Home & Topics

| Component | File | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| **HomeClient** | [home-page-new.tsx](file:///d:/Next.js-projects/answarly/components/home-page-new.tsx) | Main homepage component with two sections: **Hero** (full-height gradient with `RippleGrid` WebGL background, animated card swap showing "Customizable/Smooth/Reliable", CTA buttons) and **Topics grid** (fetches trending topics from API, renders searchable card grid with loading skeletons). |
| **TopicCard** | [topic-card.tsx](file:///d:/Next.js-projects/answarly/components/topic-card.tsx) | Compact card displaying a topic's bilingual title and description. Links to `/quiz/setup?category=...` for one-click quiz start. Has a **gradient hover overlay** with scale-up animation and elevation lift. |
| **TopicDetail** | [topic-detail.tsx](file:///d:/Next.js-projects/answarly/components/topic-detail.tsx) | Full-page topic view with gradient banner, bilingual title/description, content area rendered in `prose` dark mode, and a "Back" button. Staggered reveal animations. |

---

### Question & Quiz Components

| Component | File | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| **QuestionCard** | [question-card.tsx](file:///d:/Next.js-projects/answarly/components/question-card.tsx) | **334-line** interactive component for displaying and answering a single question in **all 4 types**: MCQ (button grid with correct/wrong highlighting), True/False (with reason reveal), Code Snippet (starter code block + user code textarea + output textarea, all with copy-to-clipboard buttons), Open Ended (textarea with character count). Auto-saves progress to an in-memory store via `setProgress()`. |
| **QuizQuestion** | [quiz-question.tsx](file:///d:/Next.js-projects/answarly/components/quiz-question.tsx) | Similar to `QuestionCard` but designed for the **quiz-taking** flow. Receives `value` and `onChange` props from the parent quiz page so answers are collected centrally. Shows type badge, difficulty badge, and category badge. Does **not** show correct/wrong — that's revealed in the results page. |
| **AddQuestionForm** | [add-question-form.tsx](file:///d:/Next.js-projects/answarly/components/add-question-form.tsx) | **808-line** mega form for creating new questions. Features: 3-level **hierarchical category picker** (root → subcategory → third level), ability to **create new categories** inline, question type selector (MCQ/T-F/Code/Open-ended), conditional fields per type (options, correct answer, code, reason), difficulty picker (Academic: Easy/Medium/Hard or Professional: Beginner/Intermediate/Advanced), and API submission with toast feedback. |
| **OptionField** | [option-field.tsx](file:///d:/Next.js-projects/answarly/components/option-field.tsx) | Reusable input row for MCQ options inside `AddQuestionForm`. Each row has a text input + "Remove" button. Includes debug hooks for development. |

---

### Search & Leaderboard

| Component | File | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| **GlobalSearch** | [global-search.tsx](file:///d:/Next.js-projects/answarly/components/global-search.tsx) | **Command palette-style** search dialog triggered by clicking the search bar or pressing `⌘K`/`Ctrl+K`. Fetches all topics on mount, filters them with 200ms debounce, shows matching topics with tags, and links to quiz setup. Shows a gradient loader during search transitions. |
| **Leaderboard** | [leaderboard.tsx](file:///d:/Next.js-projects/answarly/components/leaderboard.tsx) | Ordered list rendering user rankings with avatar circles (numbered), username, attempt count, average score %, and total score. Gradient avatar backgrounds. |

